OL,3,GNEWSACity becomes first to ban Black
OL,4,AFriday adverts
OL,5,
OL,6,FBristol has become the first city in
OL,7,Fthe country to ban adverts that
OL,8,Fencourage "excessive consumption" of
OL,9,Ffast fashion on council-owned
OL,10,Fbillboards.
OL,12,FCouncillors voted in favour of
OL,13,Fproposals that will also prevent the
OL,14,Fadvertising of non-electric cars,
OL,15,Fflights, cruise holidays and travel
OL,16,Fagents.
OL,18,FThe ban will apply to all bus stops in
OL,19,Fthe city, and some free-standing
OL,20,Fscreens in the city centre. The council
OL,21,Fcan only choose who advertises in cases
OL,22,Fwhere it owns the display.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
